              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesHadronsAsKKModesOf5dYangMillsTheory"} Hadrons as KK-modes of 5d Yang-Mills theory
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
                    %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=5
          %p
            For
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%281%29"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            this reduces to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Maxwell+theory"} D=5 Maxwell theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            this becomes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+Yang-Mills+theory"} massive Yang-Mills theory
            in 4 dimensions. Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetrization
            it becomes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 super Yang-Mills theory
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#HadronsAsKKModesOf5dYangMillsTheoryReferences Hadrons as KK-modes of 5d Yang-Mills theory
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
            in 4d as
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} holographic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK+reduction"} KK-theoretic
            reduction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 Yang-Mills theory
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahManton89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Manton"} Nicholas Manton
              = succeed "," do
                %em Skyrmions from instantons
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(89)90340-7"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(89)90340-7
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
            in 4 dimensional spacetime, with
            = succeed "-contributiuons" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson"} vector meson
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT"} holographic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            reduction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 Yang-Mills theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto04"}> Sakai-Sugimoto 04, Section 5.2
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto05"} Sakai-Sugimoto 05, Section 3.3
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16, Section 15.3.4
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Bartolini17"} Bartolini 17, Section 2
          %p
            This phenomenon is essentially the theorem of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahManton89"} Atiyah-Manton 89
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sutcliffe10"} Sutcliffe 10
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Sutcliffe15"} Sutcliffe 15
          %p
            In this way Skyrmions (and hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+nuclei"} atomic nuclei
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AsAModelForBaryonsAndNuclei"} below
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            as a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-D8-brane+intersection"} D4/D8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+model"} intersecting D-brane model
            described by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-QCD+correspondence"} AdS-QCD correspondence
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"}> holographic QCD
            ”).
          %p
            This already produces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            spectra with moderate quantitative agreement with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            (
            %a{:href => "#HSSY07"}> HSSY 07
            ):
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BaryonSpectrumInSakaiSugimoto.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16
          %p
            This way, via the equivalence between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-D8-brane+intersections"} D4-D8-brane intersections
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            in the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8-brane
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapped
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"}> Sugimoto 16, 15.4.1
            ):
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BaryonsAsD4Branes.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D2+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=2 Yang-Mills theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=4 Yang-Mills theory
            %li
