          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuji+Tachikawa"}> Yuji Tachikawa
              , Section 6.4 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=2
                  supersymmetric dynamics for pedestrians
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.2684"} arXiv:1312.2684
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-3-319-08822-8"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-08822-8
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www-hep.phys.s.u-tokyo.ac.jp/~yujitach/tmp/dummies/dummies.html#dummiesse7.html"} web version
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesHadronsAsKKModesOf5dYangMillsTheory Hadrons as KK-modes of 5d Yang-Mills theory
            %p
              The suggestion that the tower of observed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
              – when regarded as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hidden+local+symmetry"} hidden local symmetries
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral perturbation theory
              – is reasonably modeled as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+theory"} Kaluza-Klein tower
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 Yang-Mills theory
            %ul
              %li#SonStephanov03
                D. T. Son, M. A. Stephanov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em QCD and dimensional deconstruction
                = succeed "," do
